Janis Papanagnou wrote...
> It's the conflict (not so much the AC) that has this huge effect.

It's not just the conflict.  You'll notice this against lone monsters, 
where conflict doesn't prevent them from swinging at you.

> Doesn't AC:-20 vs. AC:-35 roughly mean just a potentially 7.5 pts of
> more damage if a monster hits? 

It isn't quite that simple, and it isn't a full 7.5 points of damage 
reduction.  But the increase can really add up over time.

For instance, a minotaur attacks the AC -20 character for:
3d10-d20, 3d10-d20, 2d8-d20

And the AC -35 character for: 3d10-d35, 3d10-d35, 2d8-d35

A little simulation that should work in any modern browser:

