10;j++) for(var k=1;k<=10;k++) {for(x=1;x<=20;x++) if (i+j+k-x > 0) 
a=a+i+j+k-x; for(x=1;x<=35;x++) if (i+j+k-x > 0) b=b+i+j+k-x; } 
document.write(a/20000,"<br>",b/35000);

javascript:var a=0;var b=0;for(var i=1;i<=8;i++) for(var j=1;j<=8;j++) 
{for(x=1;x<=20;x++) if (i+j-x > 0) a=a+i+j-x; for(x=1;x<=35;x++) if 
(i+j-x > 0) b=b+i+j-x;} document.write(a/1280, "<br>",b/2240);

So the first character might take about 7+7+2=16 damage per round 
and the second character about 4+4+1=9 damage. 

But that's assuming the minotaur hits on every attack, which it usually 
won't, especially against the second character.  I think it is fair to 
say that the second character takes half as much damage.  

And if he's leveled up, he'll be regenerating HP twice as fast.










